{% extends 'AdminBundle::layout.html.twig' %}
{% block content %}

<div class="block"><div class="content">
	<h2>Introduction to Languages</h2>
	<div class="inner">
		<p>
			Languages control the <span class="highlight">words and phrases</span> used in your helpdesk. By editing a language,
			you can changes phrases or create new ones to suit your needs.
		</p>
		<p>
			Many areas of your helpdesk are implemented using the language system to make it easy to translate all aspects of
			the system. For example, category titles are actually phrases in the language system that you can easily translate
			to other languages.
		</p>
		<p>
			Any language can have <span class="highlight">sub-languages</span> that inherit all phrases from their parents. This allows you to
			create similar languages that only change in some specific way (for example, maybe you only want to change 1 word).
		</p>
	</div>
</div></div>

{% if has_no_langs %}
	<div class="block"><div class="content">
		<h2>Create a Style</h2>
		<div class="inner">
			<p>
				You currently have no languages defined. This means that the default English language is always used. Create a new language
				to start customizing phrases. Don't worry, you can revert changes at any time if you make a mistake and
				the language won't be publicly visible until you choose to enable it.
			</p>
			<form action="{{ path('admin_langs_newlang') }}" method="get">
				<div class="group navform wat-cf">
					<button class="button" type="submit">
						<img src="{{ asset('images/icons/tick.png') }}" alt="Save" /> Create a new language
					</button>
				</div>
			</form>
		</div>
	</div></div>
{% endif %}


{% endblock %}
{% block sidebar %}
	<div class="block notice">
		<h4>Need Help?</h4>
		<p>
			Read the <a href="">help pages</a> regarding languages for more information about things like how phrases and inheritance work.
		</p>
	</div>
{% endblock %}